[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Two Knights Attack"]
[ECO "B11"]
[Character "solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "bishop-pin,good-bishop"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.Nc3"]
[Start "short-system 1...c6"]

2. Nc3 d5 { Same plan as always: attack e4 with the d-pawn, backed by the c6 pawn. } 3. Nf3 ( 3. d4 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 ) ( 3. exd5 cxd5 4. d4 ( 4. Nf3 { The same position as 2.Nf3 d5 3.exd5 cxd5 4.Nc3: Black plays ...Nc6. } ) ( 4. Bb5+ Nc6 { Blocks with a piece that wants to come out anyway. Black follows with ...Nf6, ...e6 and ...Bd6. } ) 4... Nf6 ) ( 3. e5 Bf5 { Out before ...e6, as in every Advance line. } 4. d4 { The same position as 2.d4 d5 3.e5 Bf5 4.Nc3: Black plays ...e6. } ( 4. Nf3 { The same position as 2.Nf3 d5 3.e5 Bf5 4.Nc3: Black plays ...e6. } ) ) ( 3. d3 e5 { Takes the centre that White has left alone. If White swaps on d5, Black recaptures with the c-pawn and has two strong centre pawns. } ) 3... Bg4 { Pins the knight to the queen and gets the bishop out before ...e6. } 4. h3 ( 4. exd5 cxd5 5. h3 ( 5. d4 Nc6 { The same position as the Exchange Variation with 4.Nf3 Nc6 5.Nc3 Bg4. } ) ( 5. Be2 Nc6 { Develops and keeps an eye on d4 and e5. } ) ( 5. Bb5+ Nc6 ) 5... Bxf3 6. Qxf3 e6 { Guards d5, which the queen and the knight on c3 both attack. } 7. Bb5+ ( 7. d4 Nc6 { The same position as the Exchange Variation line 5.Nc3 Bg4 6.h3 Bxf3 7.Qxf3 e6. } ) 7... Nc6 { Blocks with the knight. Black follows with ...Nf6 and ...Bd6 or ...Be7, then castles. } ) ( 4. Be2 e6 { Supports d5. If White castles, ...Nf6 and ...Be7 follow; Black can swap on f3 whenever the knight becomes annoying. } ) ( 4. d4 e6 ) ( 4. d3 e6 { Supports d5 and keeps the pin. White's slow set-up gives Black time for ...Nf6, ...Bb4 or ...Be7 and castling. } ) 4... Bxf3 { Takes the knight that guards d4 and e5, rather than retreating and letting g4 push the bishop around. } 5. Qxf3 ( 5. gxf3 e6 { Supports d5. White's doubled f-pawns and open king give Black an easy game: ...Nd7, ...Ngf6 or ...Ne7 and ...Bd6 follow. } ) 5... e6 { Supports d5 and opens the way for the king's bishop. } 6. d4 ( 6. exd5 cxd5 { The same position as 4.exd5 cxd5 5.h3 Bxf3 6.Qxf3 e6. } ) ( 6. d3 Nd7 { Covers e5 and f6 and gets ready for ...Ngf6. White's queen and bishops have little to aim at. } ) ( 6. Be2 Nf6 ) ( 6. g3 Nf6 ) ( 6. e5 Ne7 { The knight heads for f5 or g6, since the e5 pawn has taken f6. Black follows with ...c5 and ...Nbc6. } ) 6... Nf6 { Develops and attacks e4. White has the bishop pair, but Black has no weaknesses. } 7. Bd3 dxe4 { Takes the pawn so White cannot keep a big centre. } 8. Nxe4 Nxe4 { Trades White's best-placed piece. } 9. Qxe4 Nd7 { Black develops without weaknesses. If White varies, castle short, play ...Be7 and ...c5 to challenge d4. } *
